// A thicket the tower can push through or walk around.
//
// The cheapest possible shape of the verb: no cost, no item, just a
// choice about *speed against attention*. Pushing through is faster and
// louder; going round costs nothing but the ground you did not cover.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
WaypointDef(
    id: "waypoint.snare_thicket",
    name: "Snare Thicket",
    // Second person, present tense, and short. This is read once as the
    // thing comes into range and never again.
    said: "Thorn and wire mark an old nesting ground. Go around, or cut straight through and wake what lives there?",
    take: "Cut straight through",
    // Pushing through is the *taken* branch, so the cost is on the take
    // and doing nothing is free. That is the shape §11 asks for
    // everywhere: the free answer is always available and never the
    // best one.
    costs: [],
    gives: [],
    // Loud. Provocation is the one difficulty dial (`SYSTEMS.md` §2.6),
    // and shoving through a thicket is the noisiest thing a tower can
    // do that is not lighting a burner.
    provocation: 60,
    // And it saves ground: the tower comes out the far side further
    // along than it went in.
    paces: 300,
    // A unique, forecastable territorial crisis rather than one random
    // beat among many. Ignoring it is the detour; taking it rouses the
    // Mother, after which walking and halting remain the two responses.
    landmark_region: "region.deep_jungle",
    // Late in the first region, after the tower has had time to choose
    // between transport and one coherent defence posture. The natural
    // progression check reaches it with the starting thorn gun plus a
    // Tanglenet; a Dart Battery is the competing damage-heavy purchase,
    // not another checklist prerequisite. Earlier placement advertised
    // a granted-fixture answer the ordinary economy could not produce.
    landmark_permille: 850,
    resident: "enemy.thicket_mother",
)
